<type>(<scope>): <subject>
# Subject line: imperative mood, <= 100 chars. No trailing period.
#
# types: feat, fix, chore, perf, refactor, docs, test, style, ci, build, revert, merge
# scopes (optional): agents, bus, cli, ui, copilot, scanners, runtime, config, deps,
#                    store, triage, report, modules, hooks, ci

# --- Body ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave one blank line before the body. Explain *why* the change is needed
# and any non-obvious *what*. Wrap at ~72 chars for readability in terminals.



# --- Footer ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Blank line, then footers. Common ones:
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description of the break>
#   Closes #123
#   Refs #456
#   Co-Authored-By: Name <email@example.com>

# Activate this template once per clone:
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Bypass the commit-msg hook in emergencies:
#   git commit --no-verify -m "..."
# See docs/devex/05-conventions-assessment.md for the full escape-hatch list.
